# CTABand — the strip at the bottom of a marketing page that asks for the click
# one more time: a line, a sentence, the action.
#
#     use CTABand("Start building today.", "No card, no sales call — a key in your inbox."):
#         button "Request access" -> requestAccess(email)
#         use Link("Talk to us", "/contact")
#
# It is `Hero`'s smaller sibling and shares its shape deliberately: same centred
# column, same action strip, same `:empty` rule so a band with no actions costs no
# air. What it does not share is the type scale — a hero headline is the biggest
# thing on the page and a band's line must not compete with it — which is the
# whole reason this is a component and not a `Hero` with a `small: bool`.
#
# THE SURFACE IS THE DIFFERENCE. A hero sits on the page background; a band is a
# panel, so the eye finds it after a long scroll without needing a heading. It
# uses `--x-panel`, the same token `layout/panel.fct` and the right-rail panels
# use, so a site that restates that one variable restates it everywhere.
#
# The actions are a `slot` for the reason `marketing/hero.fct` gives: a button's
# arguments belong to the call site, an `action` reference cannot be invoked with
# them through a parameter, and a node is not an expression.
app FacetMarketing:
    css:
        [data-fa-mount] .x-cta { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center;
                text-align: center; gap: 12px; box-sizing: border-box;
                padding: 40px 24px; border-radius: 20px; border: none;
                background: var(--x-panel, #16181c); }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-cta-title { display: block; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.2;
                      letter-spacing: -.01em; font-size: clamp(22px, 3.2vw, 30px); }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-cta-sub { display: block; color: var(--fa-muted); font-size: 16px;
                    line-height: 1.5; max-width: 56ch; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-cta-actions { display: flex; flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap;
                      align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 12px;
                      padding-top: 6px; border: none; background: none; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-cta-actions:empty { display: none; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-cta-actions button { background: var(--fa-accent); color: #fff;
                      border: none; border-radius: 9999px; font-weight: 700; font-size: 15px;
                      padding: 12px 24px; cursor: pointer; align-self: auto; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-cta-actions button:hover { filter: brightness(1.08); }
        # AN `if` THAT RENDERS NOTHING STILL LEAVES ITS ELEMENT BEHIND. A
        # conditional child is its own tracked region, so `if x != "":` with an
        # empty `x` produces an empty element — which costs nothing on its own and
        # costs one `gap` inside a flex container, appearing as unexplained air
        # under a stat with no delta or over a card with no title. An unclassed
        # empty element is always a region that rendered nothing, so hiding it is
        # always right; a classed one may be a deliberate empty box (a spinner's
        # ring, a marker element) and is left alone.
        [data-fa-mount] .x-cta > div:empty:not([class]) { display: none; }
    component CTABand(title: text, sub: text):
        box class "x-cta":
            text "{title}" class "x-cta-title"
            if sub != "":
                text "{sub}" class "x-cta-sub"
            row class "x-cta-actions":
                slot
